1015:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c **** /** @defgroup ADC_Group5 Regular Channels DMA Configuration functions
1016:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****  *  @brief   Regular Channels DMA Configuration functions 
1017:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****  *
1018:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c **** @verbatim   
1019:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****  ===============================================================================
1020:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****             ##### Regular Channels DMA Configuration functions #####
1021:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****  ===============================================================================  
1022:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****     [..] This section provides functions allowing to configure the DMA for ADC 
1023:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          regular channels.
1024:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          Since converted regular channel values are stored into a unique data 
1025:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          register, it is useful to use DMA for conversion of more than one regular 
1026:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          channel. This avoids the loss of the data already stored in the ADC 
1027:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          Data register.   
1028:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          When the DMA mode is enabled (using the ADC_DMACmd() function), after each
1029:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          conversion of a regular channel, a DMA request is generated.
1030:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****     [..] Depending on the "DMA disable selection for Independent ADC mode" 
1031:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          configuration (using the ADC_DMARequestAfterLastTransferCmd() function), 
1032:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          at the end of the last DMA transfer, two possibilities are allowed:
1033:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****       (+) No new DMA request is issued to the DMA controller (feature DISABLED) 
1034:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****       (+) Requests can continue to be generated (feature ENABLED).  
1035:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****     [..] Depending on the "DMA disable selection for multi ADC mode" configuration 
1036:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          (using the void ADC_MultiModeDMARequestAfterLastTransferCmd() function), 
1037:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****          at the end of the last DMA transfer, two possibilities are allowed:
1038:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****         (+) No new DMA request is issued to the DMA controller (feature DISABLED) 
1039:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****         (+) Requests can continue to be generated (feature ENABLED).
1040:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c **** 
1041:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c **** @endverbatim
1042:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   * @{
1043:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   */
1044:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   
1045:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****  /**
1046:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   * @brief  Enables or disables the specified ADC DMA request.
1047:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   * @param  ADCx: where x can be 1, 2 or 3 to select the ADC peripheral.
1048:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   * @param  NewState: new state of the selected ADC DMA transfer.
1049:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   *          This parameter can be: ENABLE or DISABLE.
1050:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   * @retval None
1051:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_adc.c ****   */
